[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:78. The Last One]
[00:00.660] Passage 78 | 文章七十八
[00:03.175] The last one. | 最后一个。
[00:06.165] After reading an article entitled | 在读了一篇题为
[00:10.280] Cigarette Smoking and Your Health, | 《吸烟与健康》的文章后，
[00:14.085] I lit a cigarette to calm my nerves. | 我点燃了一支烟来镇定我的神经。
[00:18.460] I smoked with concentration and pleasure, | 我集中精神，享受地吸着，
[00:22.490] as I was sure that this would be my last cigarette. | 因为我确信这将是我最后一支烟。
[00:28.060] For a whole week, I did not smoke at all, | 整整一个星期，我一点烟都没抽，
[00:32.380] and during this time, my wife suffered terribly. | 在这段时间里，我妻子受尽了折磨。
[00:37.610] I had all the usual symptoms of someone giving up smoking: | 我有所有戒烟者通常会有的症状：
[00:43.170] a bad temper and an enormous appetite. | 脾气暴躁和胃口大开。
[00:47.895] My friends kept on offering me cigarettes and cigars. | 我的朋友们不停地给我递烟和雪茄。
[00:53.595] They made no effort to hide their amusement whenever I produced a packet of sweets from my pocket. | 每当我从口袋里掏出一包糖果时，他们毫不掩饰自己的取乐。
[01:01.950] After seven days of this, I went to a party. | 这样过了七天，我参加了一个派对。
[01:07.215] Everybody around me was smoking, and I felt extremely uncomfortable. | 周围每个人都在吸烟，我感到非常不舒服。
[01:13.550] When my old friend Brian urged me to accept a cigarette, | 当我的老朋友布莱恩劝我接受一支烟时，
[01:18.730] it was more than I could bear. | 我实在忍无可忍。
[01:21.215] I took one, guiltily, lit it, and smoked with satisfaction. | 我内疚地拿起一支，点燃，然后满意地吸了起来。
[01:28.005] My wife was delighted that things had returned to normal once more. | 我妻子很高兴一切又恢复了正常。
[01:34.445] Anyway, as Brian pointed out, | 总之，正如布莱恩所指出的，
[01:38.005] it is the easiest thing in the world to give up smoking. | 戒烟是世界上最容易的事。
[01:42.890] He himself has done it lots of times. | 他自己已经戒过很多次了。